---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
const law = site.jurisdiction
  ? `These terms are governed by the laws of ${site.jurisdiction}, without regard to conflict-of-law rules.`
  : 'These terms are governed by the laws of the place where the site operator is established, without regard to conflict-of-law rules.';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`The terms that apply when you use ${site.name}’s calculators and content.`}
  path="/terms/"
  updated="2026-09-25"
  lede={`By using ${site.name}, you agree to these terms. Please read them — they’re short.`}
>
  <h2>1. What we provide</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} offers free online calculators and educational articles about personal and small-business finance, taxes and
    benefits. The site is provided for general information and education only.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Not professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is financial, investment, tax, legal, insurance or medical advice, and using the site does not create a
    professional or fiduciary relationship. Calculator results are estimates based on the information you enter and on the
    assumptions described on each page. Always confirm important decisions with a qualified professional and with official sources.
    See our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to keep formulas and figures correct and up to date, but laws, rates and program rules change, and errors can
    happen. The site is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including
    accuracy, completeness, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the site for any unlawful purpose;</li>
    <li>copy, scrape or republish substantial parts of the site’s content or code without permission;</li>
    <li>interfere with the site’s operation, security or advertising, including by generating invalid ad clicks or impressions;</li>
    <li>misrepresent your affiliation with {site.name} or imply our endorsement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The site’s text, design, graphics and code are owned by {site.owner} or its licensors and protected by copyright and other
    laws. You may use the calculators for your own personal or internal business purposes and share links to any page. Brief
    quotations with attribution and a link are welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-party links and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site contains links to third-party websites and displays advertisements served by third parties. We don’t control and
    aren’t responsible for their content, products or practices, and an ad appearing on the site is not an endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.owner} will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or
    punitive damages, or any loss of profits, savings or data, arising from your use of — or inability to use — the site or any
    calculator result. Where liability can’t be excluded, it is limited to the maximum extent the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify and hold {site.owner} harmless from claims arising out of your misuse of the site or your violation of
    these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update the site and these terms at any time. The “last updated” date shows the latest version. Continuing to use the
    site after changes means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>{law} If any provision is found unenforceable, the rest remain in effect.</p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</ProseLayout>
